# AUTHORS
#
# Everyone who has contributed to this tree, in the order they first did, one
# `Proper Name <address>` per line.
#
# ## What this file is authoritative for
#
# The **name** on each line is the name this tree calls that person, and the
# **address** is the one they are reached at.  When a commit carries an older
# address — a work one, an address that changed — this file is still right, and
# the commit is the record of where the change came from rather than of who
# made it.
#
# Linux keeps that mapping in `.mailmap`, which `git shortlog`, `git log` and
# `git blame` apply automatically.  This tree does not: it has one contributor
# and one address, so a second file that folds several addresses into one would
# resolve a problem that does not exist yet.  When a second address does appear,
# the mapping goes here in the same commit that first needs it, and the form is
# `gitmailmap(5)`'s:
#
#   Proper Name <current@address>  Commit Name <old@address>
#
# until then, one line per person, no ceremony.
#
# ## What this file is not
#
# It carries no legal weight.  `NOTICE` is the file that states the copyright
# holder and the licence, and the licence of a contribution is the one its
# commit was made under.  A name here is a courtesy and a record; it is not a
# copyright claim and it grants nothing.
#
# It is also **not** responsibility.  Who reviews which part of the tree now is
# `MAINTAINERS`, and the two answer different questions: a contributor who has
# moved on stays here, and a maintainer who takes over a subsystem is an entry
# there.

Raiden Lumine <2557597107@qq.com>
